&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CVE Publication: &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-10012&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-10012&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;summary&#34;&gt;Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&#34;text-align: justify;&#34;&gt;A SQL Injection vulnerability was discovered in the &lt;code&gt;ref_cod_aluno&lt;/code&gt; parameter of the &lt;code&gt;educar_historico_escolar_lst.php&lt;/code&gt; endpoint. This issue allows any unauthenticated attacker to inject arbitrary SQL queries, potentially leading to unauthorized data access or further exploitation depending on database configuration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;details&#34;&gt;Details
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&#34;text-align: justify;&#34;&gt;The application fails to properly sanitize user-supplied input in the &lt;code&gt;ref_cod_aluno&lt;/code&gt; parameter. As a result, specially crafted SQL payloads are interpreted directly by the backend database.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;poc&#34;&gt;PoC
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vulnerable Endpoint: &lt;code&gt;educar_historico_escolar_lst.php&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parameter: &lt;code&gt;ref_cod_aluno&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3 id=&#34;payload&#34;&gt;Payload:
&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;highlight&#34;&gt;&lt;div class=&#34;chroma&#34;&gt;
