item.description:
&lt;h2 id=&#34;cve-2025-22619-cross-site-scripting-xss-reflected-endpoint-editar_permissoesphp-parameter-msg_c&#34;&gt;CVE-2025-22619: Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) Reflected endpoint &lt;code&gt;editar_permissoes.php&lt;/code&gt; parameter &lt;code&gt;msg_c&lt;/code&gt;
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;CVE Publication: &lt;a class=&#34;link&#34; href=&#34;https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-22619&#34;  target=&#34;_blank&#34; rel=&#34;noopener&#34;
    &gt;https://www.cve.org/CVERecord?id=CVE-2025-22619&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;summary&#34;&gt;Summary
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&#34;text-align: justify;&#34;&gt;A Reflected Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) vulnerability was identified in the &lt;code&gt;editar_permissoes.php&lt;/code&gt; endpoint of the WeGIA application. This vulnerability allows attackers to inject malicious scripts in the &lt;code&gt;msg_c&lt;/code&gt; parameter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id=&#34;details&#34;&gt;Details
&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p&gt;Vulnerable Endpoint: &lt;code&gt;GET /html/geral/editar_permissoes.php&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Parameter: &lt;code&gt;msg_c&lt;/code&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&#34;text-align: justify;&#34;&gt;The application fails to validate and sanitize user inputs in the &lt;code&gt;msg_c&lt;/code&gt; parameter. This lack of validation permits the injection of malicious payloads, which are reflected back to the user&#39;s browser in the server&#39;s response and executed within the context of the victim&#39;s browser.&lt;/p&gt;

